<section class="philosophy section" aria-labelledby="philosophy-heading">
  <div class="container philosophy__inner">
    <p class="eyebrow">Philosophy</p>
    <h2 id="philosophy-heading">Your novel is yours.</h2>

    <div class="philosophy__prose">
      <p>
        The tools writers reach for keep getting larger. Cloud documents,
        collaborative cursors, AI co-authors, comment threads. Useful for some
        kinds of work. Distracting for the kind of work novels demand.
      </p>
      <p>
        Marmot is the opposite. It is small, quiet, and it does not phone
        home. Your manuscript is a folder of plain text files on your Mac,
        readable by any program you can imagine and any program that hasn't
        been written yet.
      </p>
      <p>
        When you finish, Marmot exports a clean, industry-standard manuscript
        PDF you can send to an agent the same hour. That's it. That's the
        whole product.
      </p>
      <p class="philosophy__signoff">
        Write the book. Marmot will get out of your way.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  .philosophy {
    background: var(--surface-sunken);
    border-block: 1px solid var(--rule);
  }

  .philosophy__inner {
    max-width: 48rem;
  }

  .philosophy h2 {
    margin-bottom: var(--space-6);
    max-width: 18ch;
  }

  .philosophy__prose {
    max-width: var(--measure);
  }

  .philosophy__prose p {
    font-size: var(--step-1);
    line-height: 1.6;
    color: var(--ink);
    letter-spacing: -0.005em;
  }

  .philosophy__prose p + p {
    margin-top: var(--space-5);
  }

  .philosophy__signoff {
    font-style: italic;
    color: var(--muted);
    border-left: 2px solid var(--accent);
    padding-left: var(--space-4);
    margin-top: var(--space-6) !important;
  }
</style>
